{"title":"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 9","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_9\">Problem 9</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 9\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In the diagram, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/a/b4a455d533200d7dfbd00731fa8bd9e8796fb803.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle PQR$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> has a right angle at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/9866e3a998d628ba0941eb4fea0666ac391d149a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"18\" />. A square is drawn on each side of the triangle. The area of the square on side <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/7/9a7c52aff9dd9987076c0ac4fecccf59b6ed8bdb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$QR$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"28\" height=\"16\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/f/50ff9540650f0f95f80da2f6692fc8ee413e2eb3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$144$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"27\" height=\"12\" />. The area of the square on side <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/6/ec6916b50feec24773d374eaada26a95bcabc6fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PR$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/2/3629b1f1f3b22f1a3c927c7ac0467574394f17ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$169$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" />. What is the area of the square on side <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/b/7ab17967324fc2b12349c0610c6c256f4c829162.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PQ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" />?.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/7/cb78ad1eb0f2f52388460e288481e19d81cbe1de.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] usepackage(&quot;mathptmx&quot;);  defaultpen(TimesRoman()); size(200);  pen lightGray= rgb(&quot;cac7c4&quot;);  defaultpen(linewidth(1.1bp)); defaultpen(fontsize(11pt));  filldraw((0,0)--(12,0)--(12,5)--cycle, lightGray);  draw((12-0.7,0)--(12-0.7,0+0.7)--(12,0+0.7));  draw((0,0)--(-5,12)--(7,17)--(12,5)--(17,5)--(17,0)--(12,0)--(12,-12)--(0,-12)--(0,0));  label(&quot;$P$&quot;, (12,5.1), NE); label(&quot;$Q$&quot;, (12,0), SE); label(&quot;$R$&quot;, (0,0), SW);  label(&quot;$169$&quot;, (3.5,8.5)); label(&quot;$144$&quot;, (6,-6)); [/asy]\" width=\"255\" height=\"335\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/5/5e58d71240a6cfd99d315dd4e8a6c90cfac437c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 16 \\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 12 \\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 13 \\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 36 \\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"397\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A square with side length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> has area <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/b/f7b59ba357a1b54473c0c4dbe8672bb404f04770.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s^{2}$\" width=\"14\" height=\"15\" />, so the square with side length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/b/7ab17967324fc2b12349c0610c6c256f4c829162.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PQ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> has area <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/1/ef15993a361abb36fa212c6690f751e22a2a234a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PQ^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"34\" height=\"18\" />. We are given that the areas of the squares on sides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/7/9a7c52aff9dd9987076c0ac4fecccf59b6ed8bdb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$QR$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"28\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/6/ec6916b50feec24773d374eaada26a95bcabc6fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PR$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" /> are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/f/50ff9540650f0f95f80da2f6692fc8ee413e2eb3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$144$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"27\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/2/3629b1f1f3b22f1a3c927c7ac0467574394f17ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$169$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" />, respectively, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/7/0270c41505f2d7bc7af4930adf99173ae980e90b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$QR^{2} = 144$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"89\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/3/5039109fb5c7c58eb66736a17c6902ddfb4ed60d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PR^{2} = 169$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"89\" height=\"17\" />. By the Pythagorean theorem, \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/3/3e3e2e5c3c5842578e7f6188f8c375fa14fb3823.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[PQ^{2} + QR^{2} = PR^{2} \\implies PQ^{2} = PR^{2} - QR^{2} = 169 - 144 = \\boxed{\\textbf{(E)}\\ 25}\\]\" width=\"540\" height=\"28\" />\n</p><p>~Blosp\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A square with side length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> has area <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/b/f7b59ba357a1b54473c0c4dbe8672bb404f04770.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s^{2}$\" width=\"14\" height=\"15\" />, which means that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/a/68a172a8d88f538cef13050d4ccd35b3ac1d5155.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$QR = \\sqrt{144} = 12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"139\" height=\"23\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/2/d62c36572fe02302307ecc41401d0649ce560ff6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PR = \\sqrt{169} = 13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"139\" height=\"21\" />. By the Pythagorean theorem, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/6/7c6b412e6f42e14ec4596a95d0826089b051bfdf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PQ = \\sqrt{PR^2 - QR^2} = \\sqrt{169 - 144} = \\sqrt{25} = 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"373\" height=\"24\" />, so the square with side <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/b/7ab17967324fc2b12349c0610c6c256f4c829162.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PQ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> has area <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/d/85d4c22f09579bd3a43979683f24010e691217f1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5^2 = \\boxed{\\textbf{(E)}\\ 25}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"105\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~Blosp\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley\">2013 CEMC Cayley</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 8\">Problem 8</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 10\">Problem 10</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 21 (page does not exist)\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 24 (page does not exist)\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 25 (page does not exist)\">25</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=CEMC_Cayley\" title=\"CEMC Cayley\">CEMC Cayley</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017232315\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.029 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.155 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 210/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 2052/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 312/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 5408/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    7.683      1 Template:CEMC_box\n100.00%    7.683      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:36345:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017232315 and revision id 281542. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}